+## beforeSession error handling
+
+When `beforeSession` throws, the error reaches the caller as a rejection and both `onError` and `afterSession` hooks fire:
+
+- A rejection from `beforeSession` still reaches the caller unchanged, fulfilling the contract that errors propagate ([validated by: throws rejection to caller when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- The `onError` hook fires with the thrown error when `beforeSession` fails ([validated by: runs onError hook when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L50)).
+- The `afterSession` hook fires even when `beforeSession` throws, allowing a deployer's cleanup code to run; when it runs after a failed `beforeSession`, the deployer can assume that no tools were run and no provider was called, because the turn was aborted at the seam before any action ([validated by: runs afterSession hook when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller ([validated by: error still propagates after onError hook](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L300)).
+- When `beforeSession` throws, the three outcomes above hold together: the error reaches the caller as a rejection, `onError` fires, and `afterSession` fires ([validated by: throws error reaches onError and afterSession when it throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
+
